File: dataframes.info,  Node: Function df_describe T,  Prev: Function df_value_counts col,  Up: String Columns

 -- Function: df_describe (T)
     Summary statistics for the numeric columns of a table.  Returns a
     new ‘df_table’ with a ‘"stat"’ string-column labeling each row and
     one ndarray column per numeric input column.  String columns are
     skipped.

     The statistics computed are: count, mean, std (sample, n-1
     denominator), min, 25%, 50% (median), 75%, max.

* Menu:

     * Examples::

1.3.1.19 Examples
.................

(%i1) prices : ndarray([10.0, 20.0, 30.0, 40.0, 50.0])$
(%i2) names : df_string_column(["A", "B", "C", "D", "E"])$
(%i3) T : df_table(["name", "price"], [names, prices])$
(%i4) df_describe(T);
(%o4)              df_table: 8 rows x 2 cols
(%i5) df_table_names(df_describe(T));
(%o5)                    [stat, price]

See also: ‘df_median’, ‘df_quantile’, ‘df_count’


